    "source-metadata": {
      "topothink-version": "0.1",
      "format": "hypergraph",
      "kind": "target-spec",
      "description": "Target topology for speak after a rewrite that honors the issues surfaced by the audit graph (speak.hypergraph.topothink.json). This is a SPEC, not a survey \u2014 artifacts named here (voices.yaml, engines.yaml, per-engine adapter modules) do not all exist yet. The graph is what the code should look like; the code is what follows.",
      "source": "designed 2026-05-26 in response to four leaks the audit revealed: (1) voice-identity erasure under engine fallback, (2) audio-tags-vocab applied to engines that cannot consume it, (3) boolean use_gcloud unable to express three engines, (4) chunking asymmetrically wired to cloud-only paths",
      "extractor": "claude (claude-opus-4-7), designed in dialogue with Harold",
      "key-design-moves": [
        "PERSONA / REALIZATION split: 'Puck' is no longer a Gemini voice ID with a Kokoro fallback hack \u2014 it is a persona (engine-agnostic user intent) that has zero-or-one realization PER ENGINE. A persona without a realization in the active engine is honestly absent from the menu, not silently coerced.",
        "ENGINE as first-class: one config value 'engine = gemini|gcloud|kokoro' replaces the boolean use_gcloud + ad-hoc kokoro flag + mutual-exclusion triangle. No --no-gcloud needed.",
        "OPTIMIZER as engine capability, not global step: the narration-director LLM call fires only when the chosen engine declares can-consume-audio-tags. Under Kokoro it is skipped entirely \u2014 no wasted API roundtrip.",
        "CHUNKING engine-agnostic: triggered by input-size threshold alone. The Kokoro path inherits chunking instead of running one giant synth call.",
        "DATA out of CODE: persona definitions and engine capabilities live in voices.yaml + engines.yaml, not hardcoded bash arrays. Adding a persona or retuning a Kokoro blend stops being a script edit."
      ],
      "anti-reification-discipline": "No 'TTS Pipeline', 'Engine Selector', 'Voice Mapper', 'Synthesis Manager'. The n-ary has-realization edge replaces the implicit lookup table. The polymorphic sc:synthesize edge replaces the if/else branching in tts_one_chunk. Categories: containment | state_change | interactivity | reference.",
      "what-this-graph-deliberately-omits": [
        "Commit history \u2014 this is a target state, not a diff. Future commits will accrue as the rewrite proceeds.",
        "The .wrangler/ Cloudflare exploration \u2014 separate decision. Either commit to Workers as a deployment target (different from a TTS engine) or remove the cache.",
        "Test wavs and scratch experiments \u2014 they belong to the build process, not the spec.",
        "Output routing modes (--stdout, --json, -o, --show) \u2014 they were already clean in the audit; nothing to redesign."
      ]
    }
  },
